## DESCRIPTION
## Optimization with constraints
## ENDDESCRIPTION

## DBsubject('Calculus - multivariable')
## DBchapter('Differentiation of multivariable functions')
## DBsection('Optimization with constraints')

################################################################

DOCUMENT();

loadMacros("PGstandard.pl", "PGML.pl", "MathObjects.pl");

TEXT(beginproblem());

BEGIN_PGML


A soda company has found that their current can design is inefficient. Their can design uses more metal than necessary to contain the liquid in each can. If their can is perfectly cylindrical and must contain exactly [`351`] mL of soda and given that [`1`] mL of soda has a volume of [`1`] mm[`^3`], what proportions should their can have to minimize the amount of metal used in constructing the can?

The proportion ratio is [`h = `][_]{Real(2)}[`r`], where [`h`] is the height and [`r`] is the radius of the can.
END_PGML

################################################################
#
#  Answers

$showPartialCorrectAnswers = 0;
BEGIN_SOLUTION
$BR
You're finding the minimum of \( S(r,h) = 2\pi r^2 +2\pi rh \) with the constraint that \( \pi r^2h = 351 \). Solving this gives \( h = 2r \).
END_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();